<title>USA: Merck says Zocor, Mevacor nine mth sales up.</title>
<headline>Merck says Zocor, Mevacor nine mth sales up.</headline>
<dateline>WHITEHOUSE STATION, N.J. 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Merck and Co Inc said on Wednesday its drugs Zocor and Mevacor hold about 40 percent of the worldwide cholesterol-lowering market, and the drugs' combined sales showed &quot;significant growth&quot; in the first nine months of this year.</p>
<p>Zocor had third quarter sales of $725 million, a 41 percent gain over 1995's third quarter, and nine-months sales of $1.96 billion, a 47 percent rise over the year-ago period.</p>
<p>Mevacor's sales in the third quarter were $315 million, a five percent drop. Nine-month sales were $895 million, a one percent rise.</p>
</text>
